{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xf7zrogfmaqur25lhidlnukfa2g6na3jldtvkyjbe3agbwoq2vwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01VbKBfC18MoMybdTtVQPsNi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-MNe1tR/translated_rust/CONFIGS.md","content":"# CONFIGS.md — configuration surface for VALID inputs\n\nDerived mechanically from `c_src/src/lib.c` + `c_src/include/lib.h`.\n\n## Axis 0 — build-time configuration\n\n`Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]`** and the C has **no `#ifdef`/`#define` and no\nCMake options** ⇒ exactly **one** configuration: the default. Every row below is\ntherefore verified once, under `--no-default-features`, once under\n`--all-features` and once under the plain default (all three are the same\ncompilation, confirmed by `cargo check`).\n\n## Axis 1 — runtime option/mode flags the public API can set\n\nThe library is stateless; the *only* runtime mode selector is the shape-type\ndiscriminant of the lowest-level dispatcher:\n\n| flag | values the C branches on | code |\n|------|--------------------------|------|\n| `C2_TYPE typeB` of `c2CastRay` | `C2_TYPE_CIRCLE = 0` → `c2RaytoCircle`; `C2_TYPE_AABB = 1` → `c2RaytoAABB`; `C2_TYPE_CAPSULE = 2` → `c2RaytoCapsule`; anything else → falls off the switch (see `ERRORS.md` row 34) | `lib.c:294-304` |\n\n`spec_ray` (the only header-declared entry point) hard-codes\n`C2_TYPE_CIRCLE`, so the AABB/capsule modes are reachable **only** through the\nlow-level `c2CastRay` / `c2Rayto*` exports — those are driven directly below.\n\n## Axis 2 — input value classes (each float parameter)\n\n`F` ordinary finite · `Z` `+0.0` · `NZ` `-0.0` · `D` denormal (`1e-45`,\n`f32::MIN_POSITIVE`) · `H` huge (`f32::MAX`, `1e38`, products overflow) ·\n`I` `±inf` · `N` quiet `NaN` / signalling `NaN` / negative `NaN`.\n\n## Axis 3 — input shapes the code special-cases\n\nRay: `A.t == 0` (degenerate/zero-length sweep), `A.t < 0`, `A.t == +inf`,\n`A.d` unit vs. non-unit vs. zero vector.\nCircle: `r > 0`, `r == 0`, `r < 0`.\nAABB: proper (`min < max`), degenerate (`min == max`, point), inverted\n(`min > max`), one-dimensional (`min.x == max.x`).\nCapsule: `a != b`, `a == b` (degenerate ⇒ `c2Norm(0)` ⇒ NaN), `b` \"below\" `a`\n(⇒ inverted `capsule_bb`), `r == 0`, axis-aligned vs. oblique axis.\n\n## Configuration rows (cross-product, pruned to what the C distinguishes)\n\nEach row is exercised with **many randomized inputs** (fixed-seed PCG32,\n`tests/common/mod.rs`), not one hand-picked value, and compared bit-for-bit\n(`f32::to_bits`) between the C `.so` and the Rust `.so`, including the full\n`c2Raycast` out-parameter (pre-filled with a sentinel so that *spurious* or\n*missing* stores are caught) and the `int` return value.\n\n| #  | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|----|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1  | `c2V` | all value classes F/Z/NZ/D/H/I/N, randomized bit patterns | [x] |\n| 2  | `c2Dot` | F×F randomized; products that overflow (H×H); mixed-sign cancellation | [x] |\n| 3  | `c2Dot` | Z/NZ operands (sign of the zero result), I×Z (`inf*0` ⇒ NaN), N | [x] |\n| 4  | `c2Len` | F (ordinary), D (denormal ⇒ `dot` underflows to 0) | [x] |\n| 5  | `c2Len` | H (`dot` overflows ⇒ `sqrtf(+inf)`), I, N (glibc `sqrtf` NaN payload) | [x] |\n| 6  | `c2Add`, `c2Sub` | F×F randomized; Z/NZ (`0 + -0`, `0 - 0` sign rules); I−I ⇒ NaN; N | [x] |\n| 7  | `c2Mulvs` | F×F; scalar Z/NZ (sign of zero), I, N; H (overflow to ±inf) | [x] |\n| 8  | `c2Div` | ordinary `b`; `b == 0`/`-0` (`1/0 = ±inf`, then `0*inf = NaN`); `b == inf` (`1/inf = 0`); `b` denormal (`1/D = inf`); reciprocal-vs-divide rounding difference (randomized, this is where a naive `a/b` translation diverges) | [x] |\n| 9  | `c2Norm` | ordinary vector; zero vector (⇒ NaN); denormal vector; huge vector (⇒ `len = inf` ⇒ `0`); NaN component | [x] |\n| 10 | `c2Minv`, `c2Maxv` | F×F randomized; `+0.0` vs `-0.0` (ternary keeps the *second* arg on ties); NaN in `a` vs. in `b` (ternary is not commutative for NaN) | [x] |\n| 11 | `c2Skew`, `c2CCW90` | F; Z/NZ (negating zero flips the sign bit); I; N (sign bit of NaN) | [x] |\n| 12 | `c2Absv` | F negative/positive; `-0.0` (ternary returns `-0.0`, unlike `fabsf`); `-NaN` (returned unchanged, unlike `fabsf`); I | [x] |\n| 13 | `c2MulmvT` | random `c2m` × `c2v`; rotation matrices from `c2Norm`/`c2CCW90`; Z/I/N entries | [x] |\n| 14 | `c2AABBtoAABB` | proper boxes, randomized: fully separated on each of the 4 axes, touching, overlapping, contained | [x] |\n| 15 | `c2AABBtoAABB` | degenerate (`min == max`) and inverted (`min > max`) boxes; NaN coordinates (⇒ returns 1) | [x] |\n| 16 | `c2AABBtoPoint` | point inside / on each of the 4 edges / outside each of the 4 sides; degenerate box; inverted box; NaN | [x] |\n| 17 | `c2CircleToPoint` | point inside / exactly on the rim (strict `<` ⇒ 0) / outside; `r == 0`; `r < 0`; NaN | [x] |\n| 18 | `c2RaytoCircle` (direct) | unit `A.d`, ray hits front face, `0 <= t <= A.t` | [x] |\n| 19 | `c2RaytoCircle` (direct) | ray line misses (`disc < 0`) | [x] |\n| 20 | `c2RaytoCircle` (direct) | tangent (`disc == 0` and `disc` ± 1 ulp) | [x] |\n| 21 | `c2RaytoCircle` (direct) | origin inside the circle (`t < 0`); circle behind the ray | [x] |\n| 22 | `c2RaytoCircle` (direct) | hit exists but `t > A.t`, and `t == A.t` exactly (inclusive bound) | [x] |\n| 23 | `c2RaytoCircle` (direct) | non-normalized `A.d` (length ≠ 1, incl. zero direction), `A.t = 0`, `A.t = inf`, `A.t < 0` | [x] |\n| 24 | `c2RaytoCircle` (direct) | `B.r == 0`, `B.r < 0`, `B.r` huge/denormal; NaN in any field | [x] |\n| 25 | `c2RaytoAABB` (direct) | proper box, ray from outside hitting the `-x` face (branch `t0`) | [x] |\n| 26 | `c2RaytoAABB` (direct) | hitting the `+x` face (branch `t1`) | [x] |\n| 27 | `c2RaytoAABB` (direct) | hitting the `-y` face (branch `t2`) | [x] |\n| 28 | `c2RaytoAABB` (direct) | hitting the `+y` face (branch `t3`, the `else`) | [x] |\n| 29 | `c2RaytoAABB` (direct) | exact corner hits / `t0==t1==t2==t3` ties (selects the *first* satisfied branch) | [x] |\n| 30 | `c2RaytoAABB` (direct) | swept bbox rejected early (`!c2AABBtoAABB`) | [x] |\n| 31 | `c2RaytoAABB` (direct) | bbox overlaps but separating axis rejects (`d > 0`) — thin diagonal near a corner | [x] |\n| 32 | `c2RaytoAABB` (direct) | axis-parallel ray (`ab.x == 0` or `ab.y == 0` ⇒ `d == da-db == 0` in `c2RayToPlane_OneDimensional`) | [x] |\n| 33 | `c2RaytoAABB` (direct) | zero-length sweep (`A.t == 0` ⇒ `p1 == p0`), origin inside the box, origin on a face | [x] |\n| 34 | `c2RaytoAABB` (direct) | degenerate box (`min == max`), 1-D box (`min.x == max.x`), inverted box (`min > max`) | [x] |\n| 35 | `c2RaytoAABB` (direct) | huge coordinates (overflow in `c2Skew`/`c2Dot`), `A.t = inf`, NaN coordinates | [x] |\n| 36 | `c2RaytoCapsule` (direct) | oblique capsule, ray origin inside the transformed slab-bbox (early `return 1`) | [x] |\n| 37 | `c2RaytoCapsule` (direct) | ray origin inside cap-circle `a` (`c2CircleToPoint(capsule_a)`) | [x] |\n| 38 | `c2RaytoCapsule` (direct) | ray origin inside cap-circle `b` | [x] |\n| 39 | `c2RaytoCapsule` (direct) | ray crosses the slab (`yAe.x*yAp.x < 0`) and hits the flat side (`else` branch, `out->n = M.x` for `c > 0`) | [x] |\n| 40 | `c2RaytoCapsule` (direct) | same but `c < 0` ⇒ `out->n = c2Skew(M.y)` | [x] |\n| 41 | `c2RaytoCapsule` (direct) | slab crossing whose `y <= 0` ⇒ delegate to `c2RaytoCircle(Ca)` (hit and miss) | [x] |\n| 42 | `c2RaytoCapsule` (direct) | slab crossing whose `y >= yBb.y` ⇒ delegate to `c2RaytoCircle(Cb)` (hit and miss) | [x] |\n| 43 | `c2RaytoCapsule` (direct) | `\\|yAp.x\\| < B.r` with `yAp.y < 0` ⇒ `c2RaytoCircle(Ca)`; with `yAp.y >= 0` ⇒ `c2RaytoCircle(Cb)` | [x] |\n| 44 | `c2RaytoCapsule` (direct) | ray entirely outside the slab ⇒ `return 0` **after** `*out` was overwritten at `lib.c:243-244` | [x] |\n| 45 | `c2RaytoCapsule` (direct) | axis-aligned capsule (vertical `a→b`, horizontal `a→b`), `b` below `a` (inverted `capsule_bb`) | [x] |\n| 46 | `c2RaytoCapsule` (direct) | degenerate capsule `a == b` (⇒ `c2Norm(0)` NaN cascade), `B.r == 0`, `B.r < 0`, huge/denormal `B.r` | [x] |\n| 47 | `c2RaytoCapsule` (direct) | `A.t == 0` / `A.t = inf` / zero `A.d` (⇒ `d = yAe.x - yAp.x == 0` ⇒ `t = ±inf`/NaN) | [x] |\n| 48 | `c2CastRay` | `typeB = C2_TYPE_CIRCLE (0)`, randomized rays × circles — must equal `c2RaytoCircle` | [x] |\n| 49 | `c2CastRay` | `typeB = C2_TYPE_AABB (1)`, randomized rays × boxes — must equal `c2RaytoAABB` | [x] |\n| 50 | `c2CastRay` | `typeB = C2_TYPE_CAPSULE (2)`, randomized rays × capsules — must equal `c2RaytoCapsule` | [x] |\n| 51 | `spec_ray` | ordinary: mouse point outside the circle, ray origin outside, hit | [x] |\n| 52 | `spec_ray` | mouse point *inside* the circle ⇒ `ray.t` short ⇒ `t > A.t` miss | [x] |\n| 53 | `spec_ray` | ray origin inside the circle (`t < 0` miss) | [x] |\n| 54 | `spec_ray` | `mp == (r_p_x, r_p_y)` ⇒ `c2Norm(0)` NaN cascade | [x] |\n| 55 | `spec_ray` | `c_r == 0` / `c_r < 0` / huge `c_r`; circle behind the mouse point | [x] |\n| 56 | `spec_ray` | fully randomized bit-pattern fuzz over all 7 floats (incl. inf/NaN/denormal mixes) | [x] |\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7010,"cache_read_input_tokens":46554,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7010,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"403ec6da-be3e-47b1-a761-1c67d01f930a","uuid":"226a16fe-ff67-4bad-b7bc-c8ee382778ec","timestamp":"2026-08-20T15:31:11.146Z"}
