{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_4bcwibhobn7gfcwf32kdhwyvizmqnwb3zhsuuoohxn5sndm3whba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## Result: `ALL CONFIGURATIONS VERIFIED` — 89/89 differential tests pass (dev + release)\n\n### Phase A — artifacts (all in the crate root)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | all 22 `nm -D` symbols of the C `.so`; Rust `.so` exports **exactly the same 22** (diff empty, dev *and* release); undefined list is libc/std only |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **44 rows**, one per distinct rejection branch grepped out of `lib.c` (there are no asserts/error enums/null checks — the only channel is the `int` 0/1), each with a passing test |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **56 rows** = the cross-product of the one runtime mode flag (`C2_TYPE` of `c2CastRay`), 7 float value classes and every special input shape, each with a passing test |\n\nBuild surface: **no `[features]` in Cargo.toml, no `#ifdef`/CMake options in the C** ⇒ one combination; `verify_all.sh` enumerates the feature powerset mechanically and runs everything for `{dev, release}` plus `cargo check --no-default-features/--all-features`.\n\n### Bugs found and fixed in the Rust (never in the C)\nAll divergences were **NaN-payload propagation**. `ADDSS/MULSS dest,src` returns *`dest` quieted* when both operands are NaN, and gcc does **not** always make the C expression's left operand the destination (e.g. `a.x += b.x` compiles to `addss` with `b.x` as dest; `c2Dot`'s sum has the *second* product as dest; `out->t = t*A.t` has `A.t` as dest). I read the operand order off `objdump -d` of the reference `.so` and routed every `+ - * /` through `fadd/fsub/fmul/fdiv` helpers — fixing `c2Dot`, `c2Add`, `c2Mulvs`, `c2Div`, `c2Len`, `c2MulmvT`, `c2RaytoAABB`, `c2RaytoCapsule`.\n\nAlso set `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false`: rustc's UB check turned null-pointer stores into SIGABRT while the C faults with SIGSEGV; now dev == release == C.\n\n### Evidence the tests have teeth\n* `classify_aabb`/`classify_capsule` re-walk the C control flow **using the C library's own exports**, and every branch-specific row fails if its branch wasn't hit enough times.\n* Out-parameter is sentinel-filled, so missing/spurious stores are caught (this is what proves `c2RaytoCapsule`'s pre-write-then-`return 0` bug is preserved).\n* 8 injected mutations (rim `<`→`<=`, tie `>=`→`>`, `t<=A.t`→`<`, dropped pre-write, naive NaN order, …) were **all** caught; suite also passes with `DIFF_SEED_OFFSET=1,2,3,7,42`.\n* Null pointers compared by **fatal signal number** in re-exec'd children (11 cases, all identical); out-of-range enums (`3,4,255,-1,INT_MIN,…`) verified to leave `*out` untouched in both.\n* Harness now **refuses to run against a stale `.so`** (`cargo test` alone does not re-link a cdylib — this was a real trap I hit).\n\nTwo documented facts worth knowing: `c2CastRay`'s invalid-`typeB` path falls off a non-void function, so the C returns caller-leftover `EAX` (genuinely undefined — the test asserts only the well-defined parts), and NaN payloads are a property of the *build*: a `-O2` C build disagrees with the prescribed default `-O0` build on 11 NaN-only rows, so matching both is impossible."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1263,"cache_read_input_tokens":317536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1263,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"403ec6da-be3e-47b1-a761-1c67d01f930a","uuid":"b1862728-a0cb-49c1-b747-d9375ec34d4d","timestamp":"2026-08-20T16:09:36.838Z"}
